# Request patterns

After you understand a user message, update this project's pattern log. Do this for repeatable tasks only. Skip greetings, a plain yes or no, and one-off questions.

Log path: `.cursor/bro-again/request-patterns.md` in the open workspace. Create the file if it is missing. On that first create, add `.cursor/bro-again/` to `.gitignore` if that line is absent. Write only this log and that gitignore line. Do not edit project source for this rule.

Each entry is one intent. Never store the raw prompt.

```markdown
## kebab-summary
- summary: One line of the intent, written so a similar request matches
- count: 1
- last_seen: YYYY-MM-DD
- suggested: no
- command:
```

- Read the log first. If an entry already describes the same intent, increment `count` and set `last_seen` to today. Do not add a second entry.
- If nothing matches, add one entry with `count: 1`. That summary is what later requests get clubbed into.
- Counts belong to this project only.
- When `count` reaches 3 and `suggested` is `no`, answer the user first. Then add one short offer: this kind of request has come up 3 times in this project, and `/create-command` can save a command in this project only. Ask if they want that. Set `suggested` to `yes`.
- When a command is saved for that pattern, set `command` to its name.
